          <item>
           
           <layout class="QHBoxLayout">
            <item>
             <widget class="QCheckBox" name="reclusterMeanSubtractedSubdimCheckBox">
              <property name="text">
               <string>Mean-subtracted subdim (single cluster)</string>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>When checked and exactly one cluster is being reclustered, klusters subtracts the cluster's mean from each spike's features, projects the residuals onto the top N PCA components of the cluster, and feeds those to KlustaKwik instead of the full feature set. Reveals sub-structure in a cluster that the canonical PCA basis can't separate. N is taken from the N-features spin-box above. No effect when more than one cluster is reclustered.</string>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
            <item>
             <spacer name="spacer_subdim">
              <property name="orientation">
               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeType">
               <enum>QSizePolicy::Expanding</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
               <size>
                <width>40</width>
                <height>20</height>
               </size>
              </property>
             </spacer>
            </item>
           </layout>
          </item>
          <item>
           <layout class="QHBoxLayout">
            <item>
             <widget class="QCheckBox" name="reclusterChannelVarianceCheckBox">
              <property name="text">
               <string>Channel-level variance selection</string>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>When checked (with auto-select features on), recluster ranks the electrode's channels by their aggregate feature variance and turns on every PCA column of the highest-variance channels, instead of ranking individual feature columns. Keeps whole channels together so a high-variance channel's components are never split. The number of channels kept is taken from the N-features spin-box above. No effect when auto-select is off.</string>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
            <item>
             <spacer name="spacer_chanvar">
              <property name="orientation">
               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeType">
               <enum>QSizePolicy::Expanding</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
               <size>
                <width>40</width>
                <height>20</height>
               </size>
              </property>
             </spacer>
            </item>
           </layout>
          </item>
          <item>
           <layout class="QHBoxLayout">
            <item>
             <widget class="QCheckBox" name="reclusterMedianWaveformResidualCheckBox">
              <property name="text">
               <string>Median-waveform residual (single cluster)</string>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>When checked and exactly one cluster is being reclustered, klusters reads the cluster's spikes from the .spk file, subtracts the per-(channel,sample) MEDIAN waveform (robust to drift and outliers), PCA-projects the residual waveforms, and feeds the top N components to KlustaKwik. Operates in raw waveform space rather than feature space. N is taken from the N-features spin-box above. Takes precedence over the mean-subtracted feature-space variant when both are checked. No effect when more than one cluster is reclustered.</string>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
            <item>
             <spacer name="spacer_medwav">
              <property name="orientation">
               <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeType">
               <enum>QSizePolicy::Expanding</enum>
              </property>
              <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
               <size>
                <width>40</width>
                <height>20</height>
               </size>
              </property>
             </spacer>
            </item>
           </layout>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </item>
       </layout>
      </widget>
